[{"id":"952252271680770048","date":1515869608000,"rawContent":"Read something about how 100 French women (surely most of them white) spoke out *against* #MeToo and said sexual assault can be seen as a \"non-event\". Reminded me of how frequently the French frame racism as a non-event..","userId":885594949,"media":null,"username":"alwaystheself","containsBlackLivesMatter":false,"containsBlueLivesMatter":false,"containsMeToo":true,"containsClimate":false,"rollingTweetsPerMonth":1.0,"sumOfBlackLivesMatter":245,"sumOfBlueLivesMatter":0,"sumOfMeToo":40,"sumOfClimate":7,"rollingSumOfBlackLivesMatter":0.0,"rollingSumOfBlueLivesMatter":0.0,"rollingSumOfMeToo":1.0,"rollingSumOfClimate":0.0},{"id":"953339658162855941","date":1516128861000,"rawContent":"Regarding #AzizAnsari: \n\n1) There really is a difference between sexual assault and \"an uncomfortable sexual encounter that I regret.\" \n\n2) It's deeply unfair to publish the details of a booty call gone wrong under the banner of #MeToo.","userId":885594949,"media":null,"username":"alwaystheself","containsBlackLivesMatter":false,"containsBlueLivesMatter":false,"containsMeToo":true,"containsClimate":false,"rollingTweetsPerMonth":2.0,"sumOfBlackLivesMatter":245,"sumOfBlueLivesMatter":0,"sumOfMeToo":41,"sumOfClimate":7,"rollingSumOfBlackLivesMatter":0.0,"rollingSumOfBlueLivesMatter":0.0,"rollingSumOfMeToo":2.0,"rollingSumOfClimate":0.0},{"id":"953351742204338176","date":1516131742000,"rawContent":"Reminder: There's a whole lotta white privilege and simplistic thinking embedded in the co-opted version of #MeToo that's been appropriated by privileged white women and white \"feminists\", none of which was intended by the black woman who actually created the movement.","userId":885594949,"media":null,"username":"alwaystheself","containsBlackLivesMatter":false,"containsBlueLivesMatter":false,"containsMeToo":true,"containsClimate":false,"rollingTweetsPerMonth":3.0,"sumOfBlackLivesMatter":245,"sumOfBlueLivesMatter":0,"sumOfMeToo":42,"sumOfClimate":7,"rollingSumOfBlackLivesMatter":0.0,"rollingSumOfBlueLivesMatter":0.0,"rollingSumOfMeToo":3.0,"rollingSumOfClimate":0.0},{"id":"953369705879953408","date":1516136025000,"rawContent":"I should also say that as a queer woman (bisexual), there is so much to be said about communicating consent and boundaries in same sex encounters, too. While I've focused on \"men\" in discussing Aziz Ansari and #MeToo, obviously gray areas extend beyond the heterosexual context..","userId":885594949,"media":null,"username":"alwaystheself","containsBlackLivesMatter":false,"containsBlueLivesMatter":false,"containsMeToo":true,"containsClimate":false,"rollingTweetsPerMonth":4.0,"sumOfBlackLivesMatter":245,"sumOfBlueLivesMatter":0,"sumOfMeToo":43,"sumOfClimate":7,"rollingSumOfBlackLivesMatter":0.0,"rollingSumOfBlueLivesMatter":0.0,"rollingSumOfMeToo":4.0,"rollingSumOfClimate":0.0},{"id":"953643729029656581","date":1516201357000,"rawContent":"Your friendly reminder that women are under no obligation whatsoever to publicly narrate their trauma or sexual experiences in order to offer perspectives on #MeToo.","userId":885594949,"media":null,"username":"alwaystheself","containsBlackLivesMatter":false,"containsBlueLivesMatter":false,"containsMeToo":true,"containsClimate":false,"rollingTweetsPerMonth":5.0,"sumOfBlackLivesMatter":245,"sumOfBlueLivesMatter":0,"sumOfMeToo":44,"sumOfClimate":7,"rollingSumOfBlackLivesMatter":0.0,"rollingSumOfBlueLivesMatter":0.0,"rollingSumOfMeToo":5.0,"rollingSumOfClimate":0.0},{"id":"953645124617232385","date":1516201690000,"rawContent":"Your decision to publicly disclose is yours and yours alone. You don't have to do it \"for the culture\". And you certainly don't have to do it to respond to strangers on the internet. #MeToo","userId":885594949,"media":null,"username":"alwaystheself","containsBlackLivesMatter":false,"containsBlueLivesMatter":false,"containsMeToo":true,"containsClimate":false,"rollingTweetsPerMonth":6.0,"sumOfBlackLivesMatter":245,"s